#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129008 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129189 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c1723a1-c676-517c-8dc5-f2b61ba017c6" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral by Swapping the Order of Integration"}] :question/id #uuid "9b2415da-21b8-5a59-9b3f-2f30b624c36f" :question/math-academy-id "e-7194" :question/problem "Change the order of integration and evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^{1} \\int_{\\sqrt{x}}^{1 } 9\\sqrt{y^3+1}\\,\\textrm{d}y\\,\\textrm{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/10/1045aaad8025b20309b92477b4a1cf98e138064210c6fbc960c64ec26c9951df.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\::\\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\quad \\sqrt{x} \\leq y \\leq 1 \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the left boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\nx=0,\n$$\n\nand the right boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\ny = \\sqrt{x} \n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nx=y^2.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as type II region. Its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\::\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1, \\quad 0 \\leq x \\leq y^2 \\big\\},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/40/40cbaaff270daddf4b60115cc272fbc8b165b83b8823d19de2c19802617ebdb4.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{x}}^{1}9\\sqrt{{y}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}9\\sqrt{{y}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{{y}^{3}+1}[{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{{y}^{3}+1}[x\\,]_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\,dy \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{1}3{y}^{2}({y}^{3}+1)^{1/2}\\,dy \\\\  & =3{[\\frac{2}{3}({y}^{3}+1)^{3/2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[2({y}^{3}+1)^{3/2}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2(2)^{3/2}-2 \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129009 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129190 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f52a0604-77f9-51c5-948a-710c52c26fe7" :knowledge-point/title "Swapping the Order of Integration on a Partitioned Region"}] :question/id #uuid "3477b5ca-309c-5b2a-b3fd-41dfc9bbf4db" :question/math-academy-id "e-7195" :question/problem "Change the order of integration in the double integral $\\displaystyle \\int_0^1\\int_{2x}^{3-x} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm{d}y\\,\\textrm{d}x .$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/47/47f6b583b2dd059ad8df49b0ca4374a964b4a28e91eb242a0dd3c7b8476fd26e.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\big\\{ (x,y) \\::\\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\quad 2x \\leq y \\leq 3-x \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we need to split $D$ into two type II regions. \n\n![](images/35/35b4b57f26c7903189899ec284faa39bb70fb3a80397b772376358d4d86b3ec1.png)\n\nNotice that the right boundary of the lower region, written in the form $x=x(y),$  is \n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac{y}{2}.\n$$\n\nAlso, the right boundary of the upper region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$$\nx=3-y.\n$$\n\nSo, we can write $D$ as a union of\n\n$$\nD_1 = \\Big\\{ (x,y) \\::\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 2, \\quad 0 \\leq x \\leq \\dfrac{y}{2} \\Big\\}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nD_2 = \\Big\\{ (x,y) \\::\\: 2 \\leq y \\leq 3, \\quad 0 \\leq x \\leq 3-y \\Big\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2x}^{3-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129010 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129191 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb8c80f2-6dcd-568e-812b-91d39a40119c" :knowledge-point/title "Swapping the Order of Integration on a Non-Partitioned Region"}] :question/id #uuid "eab89095-f5e5-53dc-9141-0f1a876f8a13" :question/math-academy-id "e-7196" :question/problem "Change the order of integration in the double integral \n$\\displaystyle \\int_0^1 \\int_{y^3}^{1} f(x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}x \\: \\textrm{d}y.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/47/47b8a129674d4644593741607e0efd5dea1ffde45357f327e3af4e08d0bf423d.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It is a type II region, and its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD= \\big\\{ (x,y) \\::\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq1, \\quad y^3 \\leq x \\leq 1 \\big\\},\n$$\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$$\nx = y^3\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = \\sqrt[3]{x},\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny = 0.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type I region. The type I representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD= \\big\\{ (x,y) \\::\\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\quad 0 \\leq y \\leq \\sqrt[3]{x} \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/e6/e627a8750d3f5055b3936d47100fc51ae68926dfdc0c53d020638c9ef99f9b27.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{3}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388286 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129190 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f52a0604-77f9-51c5-948a-710c52c26fe7" :knowledge-point/title "Swapping the Order of Integration on a Partitioned Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f813f916-0601-5644-96e2-e5f9a5ca8427" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-x-2}^{x-2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388288} {:answer/id #uuid "78361b40-3822-5ff5-a714-d5b563b1e308" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{x+2}^{-x-2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388289} {:answer/id #uuid "90893bc6-34ed-5503-86ae-a881d5d3d411" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{-x-2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388290} {:answer/id #uuid "4472336e-1218-5ca6-aa7a-105e2edd3835" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{x+2}^{-x-2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388291} {:answer/id #uuid "ab9ac760-50be-5d7e-9dce-e8de8e4f3fdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-x-2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388292}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab9ac760-50be-5d7e-9dce-e8de8e4f3fdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-x-2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388292} :answer-field/id #uuid "53604b27-d02f-579a-aedc-0bb673c96dd1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388287}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fac1e7c0-0a06-5b8c-ba15-80235cdce89f" :question/math-academy-id "q-132564" :question/problem "By changing the order of integration in the following double integrals, express the following sum as a single double integral.\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-y-2}^{0}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y-2}^{0}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\n$$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/9a/9a539f69187276895f8f53e2107c1959fefd0aeb7126dcff049569bfc8bc49d3.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It consists of two type II regions, given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le y\\le 0,\\,-y-2\\le x\\le 0\\}\\,\\cup \\,\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,y-2\\le x\\le 0\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$$\nx=y-2\\,⟹\\,y=x+2,\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary of the region is\n\n$$\nx=-y-2\\,⟹\\,y=-x-2.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type I region. The type I representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 0,\\,-x-2\\le y\\le x+2\\},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/ba/ba9c9132c8efdb811e63bebc05e1f46bc8cbc54bcb8246072013a75d53bcb4df.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-y-2}^{0}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y-2}^{0}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-x-2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388300 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129190 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f52a0604-77f9-51c5-948a-710c52c26fe7" :knowledge-point/title "Swapping the Order of Integration on a Partitioned Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d02f7bb8-5ef2-5339-92ed-4d00eb590abf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x-1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388302} {:answer/id #uuid "7aa042a9-c9fa-5cb9-9ea5-40cd801618b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x-1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388303} {:answer/id #uuid "5be04bc3-28e6-585c-911b-70cd820bce53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x+1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388304} {:answer/id #uuid "134efa9e-3222-5310-a9b2-34d97f59aea3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x+1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x-1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388305} {:answer/id #uuid "1bd1906e-d666-5eb2-a038-16879750e5dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x+1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5be04bc3-28e6-585c-911b-70cd820bce53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x+1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388304} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a76d6c6-f79c-5e15-b460-5a7e313685d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388301}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "446a02c7-d043-54a5-9d35-72c77f70ee6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-132573" :question/problem "Change the order of integration in the double integral \n${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}-1}^{1-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/e6/e6b8889f9e8025cfca1ee0ae61b67a2f7ec9ec4aee15fab78d2f418a655bbcb8.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type II region, and its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,{y}^{2}-1\\le x\\le 1-y\\}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we need to split $D$ into two type I regions.\n\n![](images/52/52640b30ded8bf2cd19fe7860c7640bde3c8427ae8978f32fb8020b2f7215468.png)\n\nNotice that the bottom and top boundaries of the left region, written in the form $y=y(x),$  are \n\n$\\,$ $y=0\\,$ and $\\,y=\\sqrt{x+1}.$\n\nAlso, the bottom and top boundaries of the right region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ are\n\n$\\,$ $y=0\\,$ and $\\,y=1-x.$ \n\nSo, we can write $D$ as a union of\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 0,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x+1}\\}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1-x\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}-1}^{1-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x+1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268897 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129189 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c1723a1-c676-517c-8dc5-f2b61ba017c6" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral by Swapping the Order of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "481ea564-184e-5eee-bfa2-8fb2bb2ee2d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{16}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266788} {:answer/id #uuid "a83b6e24-d2a5-5db0-9ccd-aaee20fdee95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4}-{e}^{-16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267668} {:answer/id #uuid "baafeef2-8a7d-5eed-b135-3d6a094b65a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267818} {:answer/id #uuid "c3d3fbe1-a09a-5e04-97b6-73751f2420d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-{e}^{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267890} {:answer/id #uuid "e4493e91-98e1-555a-9a0a-ff8a68f4d0a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{8}-{e}^{-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268159}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "481ea564-184e-5eee-bfa2-8fb2bb2ee2d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{16}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266788} :answer-field/id #uuid "29fadffe-3310-57b0-80ee-40f2f179eb3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268472}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2241615f-0c50-5601-a5f3-153a8d9e79c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-132638" :question/problem "Change the order of integration and evaluate the double integral \n${\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4-{x}^{2}}4x{e}^{8y-{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/26/262e1b0c4e0ddf338c527b487fcadc85baac12712f91cb4c54b771e49add25b9.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 4-{x}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the left boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\nx=0,\n$$\n\nand the right boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=4-{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{4-y}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type II region. The type II representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 4,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{4-y}\\},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/48/48c874b069b55599f76a8fe1aa50c5f4db36ff8943d264a107452668d689174b.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4-{x}^{2}}4x{e}^{8y-{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-y}}4x{e}^{8y-{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{e}^{8y-{y}^{2}}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-y}}4x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{e}^{8y-{y}^{2}}\\cdot 2{x}^{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-y}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}2(4-y){e}^{8y-{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={e}^{8y-{y}^{2}}\\,{|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & ={e}^{8(4)-{4}^{2}}-{e}^{8(0)-{0}^{2}} \\\\  & ={e}^{16}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475966 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129189 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c1723a1-c676-517c-8dc5-f2b61ba017c6" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral by Swapping the Order of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04acf838-dfd5-5334-97f8-7fa942e66fe0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475452} {:answer/id #uuid "8a9f9754-8306-5ac4-b4ad-620d9f3a59d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡2-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475650} {:answer/id #uuid "a28f7432-b412-5573-afe3-367aec0ba7b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡2-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475683} {:answer/id #uuid "a4ebc04f-9119-59a3-af0b-d5a0399f055f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475684} {:answer/id #uuid "b5d5f637-b439-5a31-862f-b75cf4d380cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡3-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\operatorname{ln}⁡6-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475717}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4ebc04f-9119-59a3-af0b-d5a0399f055f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475684} :answer-field/id #uuid "37f743ed-c677-5ee3-8526-cdbc90d5f567" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475846}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cb97248a-192c-5cf9-ad2e-d068b8748779" :question/math-academy-id "q-132646" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\int }_{{e}^{y}}^{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y=$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/7e/7e0a0b1860f316f7954e85b9d7f6567d9e0c05bf316cb8af3901037abe6fd17e.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It is a type II region, and its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡5,\\,{e}^{y}\\le x\\le 5\\}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$$\nx={e}^{y}\\,⟹\\,y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=0.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type I region. The type I representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 5,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/3c/3c95dd90ad02ab708f5893e47e7d7d0c8a212c18aed1972fb1bba1362181c383.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\int }_{{e}^{y}}^{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-x)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-x)[{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-x)\\cdot y\\,{|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-x)\\,{|}_{1}^{5} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-5)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-1) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-5).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326683 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129189 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c1723a1-c676-517c-8dc5-f2b61ba017c6" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral by Swapping the Order of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07e55bd6-6c1e-596d-ac6c-9c05dbbbe44a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324044} {:answer/id #uuid "7253cc11-8000-559b-8d7c-db1c1254dd64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}+1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324921} {:answer/id #uuid "a2529f23-3645-5577-bf2f-f291f15c0558" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325347} {:answer/id #uuid "dfd7c19f-6755-5300-ba8e-f738d65b0412" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325925} {:answer/id #uuid "e0292168-bcb9-5e56-a4e8-90c71cff46ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325930}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0292168-bcb9-5e56-a4e8-90c71cff46ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325930} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b72926a-e0f8-5a46-92d9-e61a9a7ee6f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326500}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d367f5e8-a63f-5c28-8123-6c8a8a1bb138" :question/math-academy-id "q-38467" :question/problem "Change the order of integration and evaluate the following double integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{1}\\frac{3{x}^{5}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{6}+{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/a8/a85f82756c621bf88b95451f54343be863345278f361fd0f0dd82f5d01c0cb5b.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{3}\\le y\\le 1\\}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the left boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\nx=0,\n$$\n\nand the right boundary is\n\n$$\ny={x}^{3}\\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt[3]{y}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type II region. Its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{y}\\},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/82/8243a8c60e4b8b4846d330a00a090d6f93f94f17323c1d0a88d486ba77745451.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{1}\\frac{3{x}^{5}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{6}+{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{y}}\\frac{3{x}^{5}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{6}+{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{y}}\\frac{3{x}^{5}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{6}+{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3{[\\frac{2}{6}\\sqrt{{x}^{6}+{y}^{2}}]}_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{y}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\sqrt{2{y}^{2}}-\\sqrt{{y}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y(\\sqrt{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\sqrt{2}-1)}{2}[{y}^{2}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129653 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129189 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c1723a1-c676-517c-8dc5-f2b61ba017c6" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral by Swapping the Order of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "017629d6-f5b2-5b5c-9795-46c0001e34b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4-\\pi )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475447} {:answer/id #uuid "34c39f6b-c2a5-5718-bc9c-ca24f1e0d9c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8+\\pi )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475515} {:answer/id #uuid "6478e2d3-fb7a-5c05-b45c-327c0ff72c90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8+\\pi )}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475592} {:answer/id #uuid "b5a2d58c-36ab-574d-b5e5-fd1bd11ca515" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4-\\pi )}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475716} {:answer/id #uuid "d0891b4c-ffff-5f35-831c-5eceb85dcec4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8+\\pi )}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475755}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0891b4c-ffff-5f35-831c-5eceb85dcec4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8+\\pi )}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475755} :answer-field/id #uuid "462e13cc-0f6e-5f57-98bc-08e786cd92cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127399}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0f89123a-9404-5b9b-b3f7-2ab98adca8fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-38468" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{x}}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{3}+\\pi )\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/19/19d2d5698ad6b22c003b44d1a023c56ae7779a6d26345732bace3723062f6e0d.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 4,\\,\\sqrt{x}\\le y\\le 2\\}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the left boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x)$ is\n\n$$\nx=0,\n$$\n\nand the right boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{x}\\,⟹\\,x={y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as type II region. Its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le x\\le {y}^{2}\\},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/81/81596115241d43f3935ba9e055a3c748c1c1ae283aa2a6a372492ee8c68170cd.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{x}}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{3}+\\pi )\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{3}+\\pi )\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{3}+\\pi )[{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{3}+\\pi )[x]_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{3}+\\pi )\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{3}+\\pi )}{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8+\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8+\\pi )}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351402 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129191 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb8c80f2-6dcd-568e-812b-91d39a40119c" :knowledge-point/title "Swapping the Order of Integration on a Non-Partitioned Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28f091ae-71fd-5540-b0f2-8d664a9a73df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{(x+2)/2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348799} {:answer/id #uuid "313158b9-4e2f-5ff4-ba54-e89efbd12aeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{(x+2)/2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348883} {:answer/id #uuid "6020d27c-755c-5bfa-8f5d-564d8485f304" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{(x+2)/2}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349325} {:answer/id #uuid "d1c4c03d-6137-5404-88a6-01c722ea987f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2}^{(x+2)/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350288} {:answer/id #uuid "db829026-f75c-5ec1-8d99-a4a9f67338a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{(x+2)/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db829026-f75c-5ec1-8d99-a4a9f67338a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{(x+2)/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350370} :answer-field/id #uuid "315458b0-a6bf-50eb-a195-5b3f5c6e3663" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350791}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0ea5f28c-cad2-5ccc-8c96-f3d93c56996c" :question/math-academy-id "q-82196" :question/problem "Change the order of integration in the double integral ${\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{2y-2}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/06/062d32beb0cab13297c21b2eab703fd5e598191c96daa93a9c27337af95a1930.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It is a type II region, and its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2,\\,2y-2\\le x\\le 2\\}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$$\nx=2y-2\\,⟹\\,y=\\frac{x+2}{2},\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=1.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type I region. The type I representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le \\frac{x+2}{2}\\},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/54/543ffc57d0d32ae9a4bdefa87bd56deb7380061004b7737cf821117b4fb20e2f.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{2y-2}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{(x+2)/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475945 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129191 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb8c80f2-6dcd-568e-812b-91d39a40119c" :knowledge-point/title "Swapping the Order of Integration on a Non-Partitioned Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a459d01-9ed5-56d1-8350-6db0e6aae3ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2-x}}{\\int }_{1}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475477} {:answer/id #uuid "78e32947-eba9-51e0-8b4c-87164677417a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2-x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475616} {:answer/id #uuid "f135f32a-6d59-5ddd-9a2f-500aff8038ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{2-x}}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475812} {:answer/id #uuid "fa5b57f1-6e21-5370-8a4c-9d6a9dd843e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{2-x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475822} {:answer/id #uuid "fd9bdb23-1fbe-5efd-a16b-c2a57100affd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\sqrt{2-x}}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78e32947-eba9-51e0-8b4c-87164677417a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2-x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475616} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b369f9a-15dc-509e-a7b9-f81d6504e3a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475834}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8d54021f-0d37-540b-875f-4f433fa4e2b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-82209" :question/problem "Change the order of integration in the double integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/48/48a1ef0d61b8b81e2fa0649b95a329099d48a802a5339d730f2da9cf8b59f547.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It is a type II region, and its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,1\\le x\\le 2-{y}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$$\nx=2-{y}^{2}\\,⟹\\,y=\\sqrt{2-x},\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=0.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type I region. The type I representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{2-x}\\},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/22/22d41ecc443e1520035f52fefe524d88062432ab1643aa19b2e0b76185b191a0.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2-x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351403 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129191 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb8c80f2-6dcd-568e-812b-91d39a40119c" :knowledge-point/title "Swapping the Order of Integration on a Non-Partitioned Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a9fb692-301a-555c-ad0e-10c4d72cf132" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{y}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348539} {:answer/id #uuid "122080a7-7feb-5643-8bf7-93193af72f6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{\\sqrt{y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348604} {:answer/id #uuid "5cefdf6c-2b0d-57e7-8909-fec41f2a1334" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{y}}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349302} {:answer/id #uuid "741e257e-02d8-5b6b-a5bc-d8d4334e468d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349514} {:answer/id #uuid "87aa7737-616d-5dee-913d-cab4bcfea596" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349684}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "741e257e-02d8-5b6b-a5bc-d8d4334e468d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349514} :answer-field/id #uuid "33560bbc-80db-5a4c-bc90-4c53ce790874" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350795}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "22d31834-ac96-55f3-b865-c529af31084e" :question/math-academy-id "q-82210" :question/problem "Change the order of integration in the double integral \n${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/82/8287ba53b227ddc36aff486ea8d42a83203940ee265163320c19ad6cdb39089e.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the right boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{y}\n$$\n\nand the left boundary of the region is\n\n$$\nx=0.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type II region. The type II representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}\\},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/2c/2c9a41f06d7edfbad9756923d9b70f1d0ffd730350d0b7d2d0e109c1bca9f80d.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475909 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129191 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb8c80f2-6dcd-568e-812b-91d39a40119c" :knowledge-point/title "Swapping the Order of Integration on a Non-Partitioned Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06ee8955-68e7-52be-ab2d-11fb2cdedbcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{(x-1)/2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475456} {:answer/id #uuid "2d14e0cf-c866-5b21-b468-f37f95e4d3a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{(x-1)/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475505} {:answer/id #uuid "42411160-e2b2-5009-9eee-fe1c4d6161cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{(x-1)/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475540} {:answer/id #uuid "426f76c7-04fb-5fbd-affe-8ee9c5415244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{(x-1)/2}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475541} {:answer/id #uuid "bbbec340-99df-5bac-8d15-3f342fb706b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{(x-1)/2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475728}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42411160-e2b2-5009-9eee-fe1c4d6161cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{(x-1)/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475540} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1839f04-52db-5ce7-ac3e-01d49177c51f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475899}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "00b86b57-002e-5667-8521-28c6ba4d5298" :question/math-academy-id "q-82211" :question/problem "Change the order of integration in the double integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2y+1}^{3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/03/03a006f46e78ec893c21d2a871c54eeccbdb0d74b19385a6a569f787ee1bdd2d.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It is a type II region, and its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,2y+1\\le x\\le 3\\}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$$\nx=2y+1\\,⟹\\,y=\\frac{x-1}{2},\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=0.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type I region. The type I representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{x-1}{2}\\},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/d2/d27e38c7c3de8dda353151cd0347d6bead91cb19d2eb90d08dd485d77899bc27.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2y+1}^{3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{(x-1)/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475971 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129190 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f52a0604-77f9-51c5-948a-710c52c26fe7" :knowledge-point/title "Swapping the Order of Integration on a Partitioned Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20692cf1-cecd-5e87-af98-7168623cc593" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475484} {:answer/id #uuid "4914a934-b1d7-50ca-be47-fcf36e01d86a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{2-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475552} {:answer/id #uuid "80e58883-b2bd-5526-aaab-81ed5508956f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{2-{y}^{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475634} {:answer/id #uuid "d91f73b0-3181-5ce4-875e-090e6aaafe05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}{\\int }_{2-{y}^{2}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475770} {:answer/id #uuid "fddebde7-b8f3-5e88-b6f1-a2c70fa31c30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2-{y}^{2}}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475826}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4914a934-b1d7-50ca-be47-fcf36e01d86a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{2-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475552} :answer-field/id #uuid "16ea8257-12db-5556-b03a-96e1c697cec1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475835}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d9c15809-274b-5c74-bd5b-6fd325ecdfd9" :question/math-academy-id "q-82252" :question/problem "By changing the order of integration in the following double integrals, express the following sum as a single double integral.\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2-x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/20/20055a4c35ca0fdcb119e69118861d9139d23f404ecb530cf7c1b9ecf39a96d6.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It consists of two type I regions, given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}\\}\\,\\cup \\,\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{2-x}\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the left boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{x}\\,⟹\\,x={y}^{2}\n$$\n\nand the right boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{2-x}\\,⟹\\,x=2-{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration we write $D$ as a type II region. The type II representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,{y}^{2}\\le x\\le 2-{y}^{2}\\},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/77/77dda47f9036b7019f0d2ea5d72c1b81e5778e5d7108760a3b0394a213690304.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2-x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{2-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351407 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129190 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f52a0604-77f9-51c5-948a-710c52c26fe7" :knowledge-point/title "Swapping the Order of Integration on a Partitioned Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a6a76c2-d198-56fe-8b14-bc84b4037254" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{y+1}^{0}{\\int }_{-1}^{1-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348669} {:answer/id #uuid "4a0a1b18-9de6-5da8-a491-9897501581c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349120} {:answer/id #uuid "62d26b45-5e87-5a0c-8356-67624fc3d6aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{y+1}^{1-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349350} {:answer/id #uuid "6927a9d9-d8b3-594f-9198-e17687250229" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{y+1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349419} {:answer/id #uuid "7c4e6d2d-5e52-5e6d-a29f-8a6b403389c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{y+1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c4e6d2d-5e52-5e6d-a29f-8a6b403389c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{y+1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349589} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6b86343-7d2b-5c15-a63a-b8cd21148e98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351051}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dc249fce-0138-5031-8e39-5c0f2472afa8" :question/math-academy-id "q-82255" :question/problem "Change the order of integration in the double integral \n${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{x-1}^{\\sqrt{1-x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/0e/0e338b779e846bc3f5ac981c93f9cda65b63d654c1152aa423f855d12d7978d9.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,x-1\\le y\\le \\sqrt{1-x}\\}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we need to split $D$ into two type II regions. \n\n![](images/d2/d2d1df8652af81fbcb789ac05a2d1bf43f9b5b12f394159d0eb17b4ecec90042.png)\n\nNotice that the right boundary of the lower region, written in the form $x=x(y),$  is \n\n$\\,$ $x=y+1.$\n\nAlso, the right boundary of the upper region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$\\,$ $x=1-{y}^{2}.$\n\nSo, we can write $D$ as a union of\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 0,\\,0\\le x\\le y+1\\}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le 1-{y}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{x-1}^{\\sqrt{1-x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{y+1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475914 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129190 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f52a0604-77f9-51c5-948a-710c52c26fe7" :knowledge-point/title "Swapping the Order of Integration on a Partitioned Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05024068-618e-5a36-97e8-3dd5f89d2e35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{y+1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{1-y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475454} {:answer/id #uuid "2b959dd5-0210-5775-a6ce-6f9d0418f353" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{y+1}}^{\\sqrt[3]{1-y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475502} {:answer/id #uuid "31b81b57-daf9-537d-9271-494c49714a7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\sqrt{y+1}}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{1-y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475510} {:answer/id #uuid "bf4de389-d746-55d8-8f5b-1a6e10d06285" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{1-y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{y+1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475733} {:answer/id #uuid "c9a903b7-8c34-5a07-b341-ca2a13539df1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt[3]{1-y}}^{\\sqrt{y+1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475745}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05024068-618e-5a36-97e8-3dd5f89d2e35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{y+1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{1-y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475454} :answer-field/id #uuid "fadcac08-89d6-5545-838e-e0a8639a57f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475906}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0e844cdc-bfeb-5b03-bf45-d36a53583297" :question/math-academy-id "q-82264" :question/problem "Change the order of integration in the double integral \n${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}-1}^{1-{x}^{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/37/374acdaf337d1977f938fc66a19a8b933a4464f922c7e9fd45fd39a6cacf920e.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{2}-1\\le y\\le 1-{x}^{3}\\}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we need to split $D$ into two type II regions. \n\n![](images/cf/cf06c4d0e0189b8b3e3c60af788c0aa082755db9b9fab17ed0562e79e11cabe9.png)\n\nNotice that the right boundary of the lower region, written in the form $x=x(y),$  is \n\n$\\,$ $x=\\sqrt{y+1}.$\n\nAlso, the right boundary of the upper region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$\\,$ $x=\\sqrt[3]{1-y}.$\n\nSo, we can write $D$ as a union of\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 0,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y+1}\\}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{1-y}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}-1}^{1-{x}^{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{y+1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{1-y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475929 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129191 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb8c80f2-6dcd-568e-812b-91d39a40119c" :knowledge-point/title "Swapping the Order of Integration on a Non-Partitioned Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ae59dc8-d178-5424-be29-70255bcce6a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{3}^{4-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475525} {:answer/id #uuid "54a91fda-7695-5788-94ff-e4b59f55fda2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475565} {:answer/id #uuid "c5b7dc90-6bb1-5e01-b095-98e1e090d69f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{4-y}{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475741} {:answer/id #uuid "cd3a87f3-39a9-5ebb-9403-664738176275" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{4-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475749} {:answer/id #uuid "e51c6fad-6b06-55bb-90c3-d9788ef7bee1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{4-y}{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475795}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd3a87f3-39a9-5ebb-9403-664738176275" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{4-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475749} :answer-field/id #uuid "d93ef9dc-afef-559b-a1a8-13f4a2ec251b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475896}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2f7d21f4-2434-59d0-b158-63a98b31b96d" :question/math-academy-id "q-82342" :question/problem "Change the order of integration in the double integral \n${\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{4-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/69/69bff6ba843a7d93cc9c60ec0adfe5986d4eea78beeca8806ec487c64f32310a.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 4,\\,0\\le y\\le 4-x\\}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the left boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\nx=1\n$$\n\nand the right boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=4-x\\,⟹\\,x=4-y.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type II region. The type II representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,1\\le x\\le 4-y\\},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/47/47bc45edcaaa73ec6fb6010aa6d6fe35c77219b234d7f2b7210f12cec55e500d.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{4-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{4-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475974 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129189 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c1723a1-c676-517c-8dc5-f2b61ba017c6" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral by Swapping the Order of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b1155cd-f35f-5f58-8850-39c81d2ccf9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475574} {:answer/id #uuid "7c39c2ee-43ff-5cba-b1e9-66bab554cd0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475622} {:answer/id #uuid "8a2dc93b-07d2-5d02-9f1c-9af81857b7f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475649} {:answer/id #uuid "923eb37f-43b5-5b42-9f6f-7c5f6423cc9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{1}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475661} {:answer/id #uuid "a9e5f989-9f92-5708-89bc-01325d6b63d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{1}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475691}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "923eb37f-43b5-5b42-9f6f-7c5f6423cc9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{1}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475661} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e37bb84-408f-59ec-be8d-27de1ffdfa7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475848}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e49d891d-abb2-5ea6-ab4c-68e975346cd4" :question/math-academy-id "q-82353" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{x/2}^{1/2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/b6/b6b672e4776973f14b8ecff1fc35bcdd50c4229ade12ec74dc09c5327223c25f.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\frac{x}{2}\\le y\\le \\frac{1}{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the left boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x)$ is\n\n$$\nx=0,\n$$\n\nand the right boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{x}{2}\\,⟹\\,x=2y.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as type II region. Its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{1}{2},\\,0\\le x\\le 2y\\},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/09/09f6f71eaf66fe10e73b80ae59a30ddd04478de71dbe37c749674ac9f10d5bd4.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{x/2}^{1/2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}{\\int }_{0}^{2y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})[{\\int }_{0}^{2y}\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})[x]_{0}^{2y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}2y\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})]_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{1}{4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
